,"key":"K2","voice":null,"speaker":null,"addressee":"odysseus","caption":"Polyphemus tears off a mountain peak and hurls it, driving a wave that nearly beaches the ship again.","isLine":false,"act":"EMBODIED_ACTION","delivery":"blind shore figure orienting by voice, hurling landscape, remembering prophecy, and praying to his father"},{"gi":4,"at":28.74,"start":37.12,"dur":18.16,"kind":"DIALOGUE","key":"K3","voice":"odysseus","speaker":"odysseus","addressee":null,"caption":"Cyclops — if any mortal ever asks who put out your eye so shamefully, tell him this: it was Odysseus, sacker of cities, who blinded you — Laertes's son, whose home is in Ithaca!","isLine":true,"act":"REVEAL","delivery":"victorious self-control collapsing into identity-driven boasting and irreversible disclosure"},{"gi":6,"at":47.35,"start":57.8,"dur":44.68,"kind":"DIALOGUE","key":"K4","voice":null,"speaker":null,"addressee":"odysseus","caption":"So the old prophecy comes home — Telemus foretold I would lose my sight at the hands of Odysseus, and I watched all these years for a great man, not this little worthless nothing who undid me with wine. Hear me, Poseidon, dark-haired shaker of the earth, if I am truly your son: grant that Odysseus, sacker of cities, never reach his home. Or if he must, let him come late and broken, on a stranger's ship, all his comrades lost — and find trouble waiting in his house.","isLine":true,"act":"QUESTION","delivery":"blind shore figure orienting by voice, hurling landscape, remembering prophecy, and praying to his father"},{"gi":7,"at":92.48,"start":102.84,"dur":7.44,"kind":"NARRATION","key":"K5","voice":null,"speaker":null,"addressee":"odysseus","caption":"A second rock misses as the ship escapes to the fleet.","isLine":false,"act":"NARRATE","delivery":"frame the action without replacing character agency"}],"beat":{"emotion":"anguish","note":"the prophecy comes home and he is blind"},"keyGi":6,"direction":{"sign":"Bi","shot_bias":{"WIDE":0.23,"MID":0.32,"CLOSE":0.